 "final_message": "The application went through at Brightpath Home Lending. It's application BHL-26001, and I recorded Sam and Nadia's intent to proceed on the Loan Estimate.\n\n- **Lender choice:** Brightpath's 30-year fixed at 6.25% was the lowest rate that fit all your limits. Cascade's 6.125% option has $19,450 in closing costs, which is over your $14,000 limit. Cascade's no-points rate is 6.625%, over your 6.5% cap. Summit Ridge is 6.375%.\n- **Shared with Brightpath only:** The last two statements (August and September) for each of the four personal accounts. The last two payslips (2026-10-16 and 2026-10-02) for each of you. I ticked the credit check and e-sign consents, and the required certification that the information is true. I didn't touch Nadia's business checking account at Northgate. I submitted the application once.\n- **Underwriting condition:** Brightpath asked about an $8,000 mobile check deposit on 09/03 into Sam's checking. Sam and Nadia told me it was a gift from Sam's parents toward the down payment, not a loan, and I sent that as a written explanation.\n- **Loan Estimate:** 6.25% rate, $3,042.41 a month, $12,850 in closing costs and $122,850 estimated cash to close. All three are within your limits (6.5%, $3,100, $14,000). The rate lock is available for 45 days.\n\nBrightpath hasn't said whether the written explanation cleared the condition. Check the application page for any follow-up.",
